  "note": "The household of Robert Evans, architect, surveyor and justice of the peace, on the 1891 return, transcribed by A. Hagues and placed at 2 South Road (#381), where the record already files Robert Evans Sr in 1911. 2 South Road held no census before 1911.\n\nThe family was already in the record without 1891, and each is bound by number: Robert Evans Sr (#405), and his children Edith Mary (#422), Alice (#423, 'Alice Ann'), Robert (#406, Robert Evans Jr, architect), Ethel (#424, 'Ethel Frances'), Mary (#425) and Dorothy (#426). The four servants and the visitor, Beatrice Elizabeth Clay, are new. The record also holds a second Robert Evans Jr, 'Robert Junior Evans' (#856, born 1863, at Ravine House in 1911), who is the same man and wants merging into #406.\n\nWright's Directory of Nottingham prints 'Robt. Evans, Esq, J.P., of Evans & Jolley' on South Road in 1894-95 and 1898-99, and 'Evans Robert J.P. (Evans & Son); h. South rd. Park' in 1910-11, without a number. Ages are as the enumerator wrote them, so a birth year worked back from one may be a year out either way.",
